<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Samoan, a draft not yet read by a fluent reviewer (#495). The notes on each string are in values/strings.xml.
    Written with the ʻokina (U+02BB) and macrons; the driver is "ʻoe", everyday register.
    "Vehicle" is taʻavale, never the word for bus; "route" is auala; "run" is taʻamilosaga; "trip" is malaga;
    "stop" is taofiga; "block" is poloka; "agency" is kamupani; "dispatcher" is le ofisa (the office);
    "report" is lipoti; "location" is nofoaga; "schedule" and "timetable" are faʻasologa o taimi;
    sign in / sign out are saini i totonu / saini i fafo; "server", "app" and "GPS" stay as loanwords.
    Samoan has no CLDR plural rules, so each plurals has only "other", worded to read right for any count.
-->
